        "custom_liquid": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Carrol Boyes Competitions | Standard Terms & Conditions (UK)</title>\n\n<!-- Poppins font -->\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@400;500;600&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\n<style>\n  /* Shared Carrol Boyes styling */\n  .cb-container {\n    font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;\n    color: #333;\n    max-width: 900px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    padding: 2rem 1.5rem;\n  }\n  .cb-container h1, .cb-container h2, .cb-container h3 {\n    font-weight: 600;\n    margin: 1.6em 0 0.6em;\n    opacity: 0;\n    transform: translateY(10px);\n    animation: fadeInUp 0.8s ease forwards;\n  }\n  .cb-container p,\n  .cb-container li {\n    font-size: 16px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n  }\n  ul, ol { margin: 0.4em 0 1.1em 1.2em; }\n  .cb-note { font-size: 0.95em; opacity: 0.85; }\n  .cb-muted { color: #444; }\n\n  /* Links */\n  .cb-container a {\n    color: #555;\n    text-decoration: underline;\n    transition: color .25s ease, text-decoration-color .25s ease;\n  }\n  .cb-container a:hover {\n    color: #000;\n    text-decoration-color: #000;\n  }\n\n  @media (min-width: 768px) {\n    .cb-container { padding: 3rem 2rem; }\n  }\n\n  /* Subtle fades */\n  @keyframes fadeIn { to { opacity: 1; } }\n  @keyframes fadeInUp { to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"cb-container\">\n  <h1>Carrol Boyes Competitions | Standard Terms &amp; Conditions (UK)</h1>\n\n  <h2>Promoter</h2>\n  <p>The promoter is Carrol Boyes (Pty) Ltd (the “Promoter”). For queries, contact <a href=\"mailto:customercare@carrolboyes.com\">customercare@carrolboyes.com</a>. Promotions are administered in accordance with the UK Code of Non-broadcast Advertising and Direct &amp; Promotional Marketing (CAP Code, Section 8).</p>\n\n  <h2>Eligibility</h2>\n  <p>Unless otherwise stated in the specific rules, promotions are open to UK residents aged 18+. Employees, contractors and agents of the Promoter (and their immediate families/households) are not eligible. Proof of age and eligibility may be required.</p>\n\n  <h2>Opening/closing &amp; how to enter</h2>\n  <p>Each promotion’s opening and closing dates/times, entry route(s) (e.g., web form, email, social), any entry limits, and any skill requirement will be stated in the specific rules or the promotional material. Entries received after the closing date will not be accepted.</p>\n\n  <h2>Free entry routes &amp; “purchase necessary”</h2>\n  <p>If a promotion involves chance (a prize draw) and an entry would otherwise require payment or purchase, a free entry route will be provided and stated clearly (e.g., standard-rate email/post). Northern Ireland requirements may differ; where NI is included, a no-purchase/normal-rate route will be offered and explained.</p>\n\n  <h2>Fairness &amp; clarity</h2>\n  <p>Significant conditions (eligibility, dates, number/nature of prizes, entry limits, how winners are chosen, and restrictions) will be clearly communicated upfront in the promotional material and/or specific rules.</p>\n\n  <h2>Entry validity</h2>\n  <p>Incomplete, illegible, bulk, automated or manipulated entries (scripts, macros, bots) are invalid and may be disqualified. The Promoter is not responsible for entries lost, delayed, misdirected or corrupted due to network/technical issues; proof of sending is not proof of receipt.</p>\n\n  <h2>Judging / winner selection</h2>\n  <h3>Prize draws (chance)</h3>\n  <p>Winners will be selected at random by a verifiably random computer process or by/under the supervision of an independent person, and recorded.</p>\n\n  <h3>Competitions (skill)</h3>\n  <p>Valid entries will be judged against the stated criteria by a competent judge or panel including at least one independent judge where required; ties and reserves handled per the specific rules.</p>\n\n  <h2>Prizes</h2>\n  <p>Prizes are as described; if unavailable, a reasonable equivalent of equal or greater value may be substituted. Prizes are non-transferable and not redeemable for cash, unless the specific rules state otherwise. Prizes will normally be awarded within 30 days of winner verification unless stated.</p>\n\n  <h2>Winner notification &amp; claiming</h2>\n  <p>We will attempt to contact winners within the timeframe stated (usually within 14 days of the draw/judging) using the details provided on entry. Winners may be required to verify identity/eligibility before a prize is awarded. If a winner cannot be contacted, fails verification, or does not claim within the stated period, the prize may be forfeited and an alternate winner selected.</p>\n\n  <h2>Publication of winners</h2>\n  <p>To demonstrate that a valid award took place, we may publish or make available the surname and county of major prize winners (and, if applicable, winning entries) unless a winner objects or we are required by law not to do so. Winners will be informed about this at the point of entry and may object on privacy grounds; in that case, the information will still be provided to the ASA on request.</p>\n\n  <h2>Conduct</h2>\n  <p>The Promoter may disqualify any entrant or withhold a prize if it reasonably believes there has been breach of these terms, cheating, fraud, or unfair manipulation of the promotion.</p>\n\n  <h2>Availability &amp; changes</h2>\n  <p>The Promoter will make a reasonable estimate of demand and will not unduly delay or withdraw a promotion. Where necessary, and for reasons beyond its control, the Promoter may suspend or amend a promotion, but will avoid unfair detriment to entrants and will communicate changes clearly.</p>\n\n  <h2>Liability</h2>\n  <p>Nothing excludes or limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, fraud, or other liability that cannot be limited by law. Subject to that, the Promoter is not responsible for: (a) entries or claims that are late, lost, misdirected, damaged or incomplete; (b) any loss not caused by the Promoter’s breach; or (c) business losses or losses that were not foreseeable. This clause does not affect your statutory rights.</p>\n\n  <h2>Data protection &amp; marketing</h2>\n  <p>We will process entrants’ personal data to administer the promotion (select, verify and contact winners; deliver prizes) under legitimate interests/contract. Any direct marketing will only be sent with consent (or soft-opt-in where permitted), with a clear opt-out. Winners’ details may be published/made available as above. See our <a href=\"/pages/privacy-policy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Privacy Notice</a> and <a href=\"/pages/cookie-policy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cookie Policy</a> for more information.</p>\n\n  <h2>Governing law</h2>\n  <p>These terms (and any dispute/claim) are governed by the laws of England and Wales, and the courts of England and Wales have non-exclusive jurisdiction; if you live elsewhere in the UK, you may bring proceedings in your home jurisdiction.</p>\n\n  <h2>Acceptance</h2>\n  <p>Participation in a promotion constitutes acceptance of these terms and the specific rules. In the event of conflict, the specific rules prevail.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"cb-note cb-muted\">Promoter contact: <a href=\"mailto:customercare@carrolboyes.com\">customercare@carrolboyes.com</a></p>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
